  "recovery_latency_s": 195.65580224990845,
  "client_view_text": " Here\u2019s a write-ahead log:\n\nHere is what the database has stored in memory before the crash:\n\nStore in memory\n\n| user_id | name | age |\n|---------|------|-----|\n| 1       | John | 28  |\n| 2       | Jane | 30  |\n\nThe write-ahead log contains:\n\nWrite-ahead log\n\n| user_id | name | age | operation |\n|---------|------|-----|-----------|\n| 1       | John | 28  | insert    |\n| 2       | Jane | 30  | insert    |\n| 1       | John | 29  | update    |\n| 1       | John | 30  | delete    |\n\nThe database crashes before the changes made in the memory are written to the disk.\n\nWhen the database is restarted, it reads the write-ahead log.  The first entry is an \u201cinsert\u201d operation for user_id 1, but that operation has already been made in the memory.  The database sees that the operation has been made, so it skips it.  The second entry is an \u201cinsert\u201d operation for user_id 2, and that operation has not been made in the memory, so the database makes the operation again.\n\nThe third entry"
}